cat > inputs/invoice.md <<'EOF'
# The invoice

The header of one invoice: who bills whom, its number and dates, and the
terms every amount is computed on. Take each value from the seller's
records; none of them is computed.

- **number** is the seller's invoice number, unique among their invoices.
- **issue_date** is the day the invoice is issued; **due_date**, when
  given, the day payment is due. Both are `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- **currency** is the ISO 4217 code every line item's price is in. The
  invoice prints amounts with two decimal places, so a currency without
  cents, such as JPY, prints `.00`.
- **tax_rate** is the percentage charged on the subtotal, after every
  discount line. Leave it out, or give 0, when no tax is charged: the
  invoice then prints no tax line. **tax_label** names it (VAT, GST).
- **seller** and **bill_to** each hold a **name**, and optionally an
  **address** (one line per line of the address), an **email** and a
  **tax_id**.
- **payment_terms** and **notes** are printed at the foot, as written.
EOF
cat > inputs/line_items.md <<'EOF'
# The line items

What the invoice bills, one item per row, printed in the order given.
As CSV, the header row is `description,quantity,unit,unit_price`; leave
`unit` empty where it does not apply.

- **description** says what the item is, as the customer should read it.
- **quantity** is how many units are billed. It must be more than zero;
  fractions such as 1.5 hours are allowed.
- **unit** is what one unit is (hours, pcs), printed after the quantity.
- **unit_price** is the price of one unit, to the cent, in the invoice's
  currency. A negative price is a discount or credit: it reduces the
  subtotal, and tax is charged on what remains.

Each line's amount is quantity times unit price, rounded to the cent. The
subtotal is the sum of the lines' amounts.
EOF
cat > templates/money.html.liquid <<'EOF'
{%- comment %}
Writes an integer number of cents as 1,234,567.89, with a leading minus
when negative. Takes cents:.
{% endcomment -%}
{%- assign c = cents | abs -%}
{%- assign whole = c | divided_by: 100 -%}
{%- assign frac = c | modulo: 100 | prepend: "0" | slice: -2, 2 -%}
{%- assign grouped = "" -%}
{%- for i in (1..5) -%}
  {%- assign group = whole | modulo: 1000 -%}
  {%- assign whole = whole | divided_by: 1000 -%}
  {%- if whole > 0 -%}
    {%- assign group = group | prepend: "00" | slice: -3, 3 -%}
    {%- assign grouped = group | prepend: "," | append: grouped -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign grouped = group | append: grouped -%}
    {%- break -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if cents < 0 %}&minus;{% endif -%}
{{- grouped }}.{{ frac -}}
EOF
cat > templates/invoice.html.liquid <<'EOF'
{%- comment %}
Every amount is computed in integer cents: a line's is its quantity times
its unit price, rounded; the tax is the subtotal times the rate, rounded.
{% endcomment -%}
{%- assign inv = inputs.invoice -%}
{%- assign subtotal = 0 -%}
{%- for item in inputs.line_items -%}
  {%- assign line = item.unit_price | times: 100 | times: item.quantity | round -%}
  {%- assign subtotal = subtotal | plus: line -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign tax = subtotal | times: inv.tax_rate | divided_by: 100.0 | round -%}
{%- assign total = subtotal | plus: tax -%}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Invoice {{ inv.number }} — {{ inv.seller.name }}</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink: #1f2328; --muted: #656d76; --rule: #d0d7de; --band: #f6f8fa; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 2.5rem 1rem; background: #eef1f4; color: var(--ink);
         font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
  .sheet { max-width: 52rem; margin: 0 auto; background: #fff; padding: 3rem;
           border-radius: 6px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.12); }
  header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; align-items: flex-start; }
  h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 2rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .meta { margin: .5rem 0 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto auto; gap: .1rem 1rem; }
  .meta dt { color: var(--muted); }
  .meta dd { margin: 0; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .parties { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 2rem; }
  .party h2 { margin: 0 0 .25rem; font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .08em;
              text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .party p { margin: 0; }
  .party .name { font-weight: 600; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  th { text-align: left; font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
       color: var(--muted); background: var(--band); padding: .6rem .75rem; }
  td { padding: .6rem .75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
  .num { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .totals { margin-left: auto; width: min(100%, 22rem); margin-top: 1rem; }
  .totals td { border: 0; padding: .3rem .75rem; }
  .totals .due td { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.1rem; padding-top: .6rem; }
  footer { margin-top: 2.5rem; color: var(--muted); }
  footer h2 { font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 1.25rem 0 .25rem; }
  footer p { margin: 0; }
  @media print {
    body { background: #fff; padding: 0; }
    .sheet { box-shadow: none; padding: 0; max-width: none; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="sheet">
<header>
  <div>
    <h1>Invoice</h1>
    <dl class="meta">
      <dt>Number</dt><dd>{{ inv.number }}</dd>
      <dt>Issued</dt><dd><time datetime="{{ inv.issue_date }}">{{ inv.issue_date | date: "%B %-d, %Y" }}</time></dd>
{%- if inv.due_date %}
      <dt>Due</dt><dd><time datetime="{{ inv.due_date }}">{{ inv.due_date | date: "%B %-d, %Y" }}</time></dd>
{%- endif %}
      <dt>Currency</dt><dd>{{ inv.currency }}</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <div class="party">
    <p class="name">{{ inv.seller.name }}</p>
{%- render "party.html.liquid", party: inv.seller %}
  </div>
</header>

<section class="parties">
  <div class="party">
    <h2>Bill to</h2>
    <p class="name">{{ inv.bill_to.name }}</p>
{%- render "party.html.liquid", party: inv.bill_to %}
  </div>
</section>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Description</th><th class="num">Qty</th><th class="num">Unit price</th><th class="num">Amount</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
{%- for item in inputs.line_items %}
{%- assign price = item.unit_price | times: 100 | round %}
{%- assign line = item.unit_price | times: 100 | times: item.quantity | round %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ item.description }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ item.quantity }}{% if item.unit %} {{ item.unit }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{% render "money.html.liquid", cents: price %}</td>
      <td class="num">{% render "money.html.liquid", cents: line %}</td>
    </tr>
{%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<table class="totals">
  <tr><td>Subtotal</td><td class="num">{% render "money.html.liquid", cents: subtotal %}</td></tr>
{%- if inv.tax_rate > 0 %}
  <tr><td>{{ inv.tax_label }} ({{ inv.tax_rate }}%)</td><td class="num">{% render "money.html.liquid", cents: tax %}</td></tr>
{%- endif %}
  <tr class="due"><td>Amount due</td><td class="num">{{ inv.currency }} {% render "money.html.liquid", cents: total %}</td></tr>
</table>

{%- if inv.payment_terms or inv.notes %}
<footer>
{%- if inv.payment_terms %}
  <h2>Payment terms</h2>
  <p>{{ inv.payment_terms | escape | newline_to_br | safe }}</p>
{%- endif %}
{%- if inv.notes %}
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>{{ inv.notes | escape | newline_to_br | safe }}</p>
{%- endif %}
</footer>
{%- endif %}
</main>
</body>
</html>
EOF
cat > templates/party.html.liquid <<'EOF'
{%- comment %} A party's address, email and tax ID, each when given. Takes party:. {% endcomment -%}
{%- if party.address %}
    <p>{{ party.address | escape | newline_to_br | safe }}</p>
{%- endif %}
{%- if party.email %}
    <p><a href="mailto:{{ party.email }}">{{ party.email }}</a></p>
{%- endif %}
{%- if party.tax_id %}
    <p>Tax ID: {{ party.tax_id }}</p>
{%- endif -%}
EOF
